## 3. i18n Implementation Details

### 3.1 i18n Configuration (`src/lib/i18n.ts`)

```typescript
export const i18n = {
  defaultLocale: 'en',
  locales: ['en', 'zh'],
} as const;

export type Locale = (typeof i18n)['locales'][number];

export function isValidLocale(lang: string): lang is Locale {
  return i18n.locales.includes(lang as Locale);
}
```

### 3.2 Dictionary Loader (`src/app/[lang]/dictionaries.ts`)

Following the official Next.js 16 pattern exactly:

```typescript
const dictionaries = {
  en: () => import('@/dictionaries/en.json').then((m) => m.default),
  zh: () => import('@/dictionaries/zh.json').then((m) => m.default),
};

export type Locale = keyof typeof dictionaries;

export const hasLocale = (locale: string): locale is Locale =>
  locale in dictionaries;

export const getDictionary = async (locale: Locale) => dictionaries[locale]();
```

Note: Do NOT import `server-only` here -- it is incompatible with static export.

### 3.3 Root Page Language Detection (`src/app/page.tsx`)

This must be a `'use client'` component since it needs `navigator.language`:

```typescript
'use client';

import { useEffect } from 'react';
import { useRouter } from 'next/navigation';
import { i18n } from '@/lib/i18n';

export default function RootPage() {
  const router = useRouter();

  useEffect(() => {
    const browserLang = navigator.language.toLowerCase();
    // Check for zh-TW, zh-Hant, zh, etc.
    const locale = browserLang.startsWith('zh')
      ? 'zh'
      : i18n.defaultLocale;
    router.replace(`/${locale}`);
  }, [router]);

  // Minimal loading state while redirecting
  return (
    <div className="flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center">
      <div className="animate-pulse">Loading...</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 3.4 Lang-Aware Layout (`src/app/[lang]/layout.tsx`)

```typescript
import { i18n } from '@/lib/i18n';
import Header from '@/components/layout/Header';
import Footer from '@/components/layout/Footer';
import { getDictionary, hasLocale } from './dictionaries';
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation';

export async function generateStaticParams() {
  return i18n.locales.map((lang) => ({ lang }));
}

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: PageProps<'/[lang]'>) {
  const { lang } = await params;
  if (!hasLocale(lang)) return {};
  const dict = await getDictionary(lang);
  return {
    title: dict.meta.siteTitle,
    description: dict.meta.siteDescription,
  };
}

export default async function LangLayout({
  children,
  params,
}: LayoutProps<'/[lang]'>) {
  const { lang } = await params;
  if (!hasLocale(lang)) notFound();
  const dict = await getDictionary(lang);

  return (
    <>
      <Header lang={lang} dict={dict.nav} />
      <main>{children}</main>
      <Footer lang={lang} dict={dict.footer} />
    </>
  );
}
```

### 3.5 Root Layout (`src/app/layout.tsx`)

The root layout must be minimal since it wraps both the `/` redirect page and all `[lang]` pages:

```typescript
import type { Metadata } from 'next';
import { Noto_Sans_TC, Inter } from 'next/font/google';
import './globals.css';

const inter = Inter({
  variable: '--font-inter',
  subsets: ['latin'],
});

const notoSansTC = Noto_Sans_TC({
  variable: '--font-noto-sans-tc',
  subsets: ['latin'],
  weight: ['400', '500', '700'],
});

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Find Nepal Trek | 發現尼泊爾',
  description: 'Expert guidance for unforgettable Nepal adventures',
};

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body className={`${inter.variable} ${notoSansTC.variable} antialiased`}>
        {children}
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

**Important font decision**: Use `Inter` for English text and `Noto Sans TC` for Traditional Chinese. Both are set as CSS variables so Tailwind can reference them. The `lang` attribute on `<html>` is deliberately omitted here (it cannot be dynamic at root level with static export since both `/en` and `/zh` share this root layout). Instead, each page can set `lang` contextually if needed via the `[lang]/layout.tsx` (though note the `<html>` tag is defined in the root layout -- see alternative approach in section 3.6).

### 3.6 Alternative: `html lang` attribute

Since the `<html>` element must live in the root layout and cannot be duplicated in `[lang]/layout.tsx`, and the root page `/` doesn't have a specific lang, the cleanest approach is:

- Root layout renders `<html lang="en">` as default
- Add a small client component `HtmlLangSetter` that runs in `[lang]/layout.tsx` to update `document.documentElement.lang` via `useEffect`. This is a progressive enhancement for accessibility.

```typescript
// src/components/layout/HtmlLangSetter.tsx
'use client';
import { useEffect } from 'react';

export default function HtmlLangSetter({ lang }: { lang: string }) {
  useEffect(() => {
    document.documentElement.lang = lang;
  }, [lang]);
  return null;
}
```

